            {
                "entry_id": "81fed10d-fea9-3836-9ec9-a81cf8eb479e",
                "word": "Saturnalia",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "8da43a0b-24b4-441a-bdae-2922e7f572bf",
                        "entry_id": "81fed10d-fea9-3836-9ec9-a81cf8eb479e",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "Saturnalias"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d30289d2-0960-3cec-bfff-715d9cea4ada",
                        "entry_id": "81fed10d-fea9-3836-9ec9-a81cf8eb479e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Alternative letter-case form of saturnalia."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "alt-of"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6b8df477-6c99-43cc-ac49-3b7709fbbbc1",
                                "sense_id": "d30289d2-0960-3cec-bfff-715d9cea4ada",
                                "text": "It was odd that the literary festival should be turned into a Donnybrook fair, but so it was when I was a boy, and the tents and the shows and the crowds on the Common were to the promiscuous many the essential parts of the great occasion. They had been so for generations, and it was only gradually that the Cambridge Saturnalia were replaced by the decencies and solemnities of the present sober anniversary."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6cf1def5-496b-4952-9578-4f6a49be8840",
                                "sense_id": "d30289d2-0960-3cec-bfff-715d9cea4ada",
                                "text": "For New York Times photographers, it has been a night to leave their families in order to document the Saturnalia of Times Square."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "72765fc8-160e-4465-9ec3-fb4a9d1ec499",
                                "sense_id": "d30289d2-0960-3cec-bfff-715d9cea4ada",
                                "text": "G N’ R, as they are colloquially known, were an affront to the ears and nostrils of civilised society, a Saturnalia in the flesh and in the speakers."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "5b302ae8-2e2a-346e-9453-4dc463db8425",
                "word": "saturnalia",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "1a450e9e-6533-459f-88e1-087f6d1942e1",
                        "entry_id": "5b302ae8-2e2a-346e-9453-4dc463db8425",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "saturnalias"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cd026280-796f-370c-bd17-60b1a1ab3d85",
                        "entry_id": "5b302ae8-2e2a-346e-9453-4dc463db8425",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A period or occasion of general license, in which the passions or vices have riotous indulgence; a period of unrestrained revelry."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "db1a8b61-bafa-4f5f-8505-878aba0b1410",
                                "sense_id": "cd026280-796f-370c-bd17-60b1a1ab3d85",
                                "text": "a man who mounts the Hustings, must not allow himself to be sore-boned, or he invites his opponents to 'touch him on the raw,' not in the exercise of their malice, but their power; an election is a saturnalia.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "80181971-d26a-43ce-a7e9-5c8281117cef",
                                "sense_id": "cd026280-796f-370c-bd17-60b1a1ab3d85",
                                "text": "They lodged men and women on the same floor; and with the night there began a saturnalia of debauchery—scenes such as never before had been witnessed in America."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c115da79-dfd1-4452-96a5-fbffea532a7f",
                                "sense_id": "cd026280-796f-370c-bd17-60b1a1ab3d85",
                                "text": "If at the birth of the Latin kings their fathers were really unknown, the fact points either to a general looseness of life in the royal family or to a special relaxation of moral rules on certain occasions, when men and women reverted for a season to the licence of an earlier age. Such Saturnalias are not uncommon at some stages of social evolution."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3ec06f23-26da-42f0-9648-7dcc1547baed",
                                "sense_id": "cd026280-796f-370c-bd17-60b1a1ab3d85",
                                "text": "Yet if he remained, it would simply mean that his own and Hagthorpe's crews would join in the saturnalia and increase the hideousness of events now inevitable."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e4a74151-a5c6-4d9f-8836-fd3c548fb7d4",
                                "sense_id": "cd026280-796f-370c-bd17-60b1a1ab3d85",
                                "text": "It was a raw, violent, guzzling saturnalia that spilled obstreperously through the woods to the officers' club and spread up into the hills toward the hospital and the antiaircraft-gun emplacements."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d0b20f18-320c-4fcb-953e-a46b4ef50736",
                                "sense_id": "cd026280-796f-370c-bd17-60b1a1ab3d85",
                                "text": "We advanced into the main hall, already aroar with a saturnalia of sozzled gestures and gibbering."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ce5c5f79-0711-4688-af58-816efce320fc",
                        "source_entry_id": "5b302ae8-2e2a-346e-9453-4dc463db8425",
                        "source_sense_id": "cd026280-796f-370c-bd17-60b1a1ab3d85",
                        "source_sense_description": "unrestrained revelry",
                        "target_lang_word": "разгу́л",
                        "target_lang_code": "ru",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "разгу́л",
                                "target_lang_code": "ru",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eb0b169d-8ba4-3c24-a302-6a4397da3e53",
                                        "entry_id": "8f41dded-98a8-339e-a1dc-99bdf3b054dd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "действие по значению гл. разгуляться; сильное, ничем не сдерживаемое проявление чего-либо"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "375b9f0f-e4f0-467b-9df8-eb5dd028a792",
                                                "sense_id": "eb0b169d-8ba4-3c24-a302-6a4397da3e53",
                                                "text": "Было что-то потрясающее в этом разгуле зимней бури, в этих бешеных порывах ветра, в этой дикой пляске моря и его закружившихся валов."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "19fc3caf-b0fc-45ce-9ebe-eb9f93c63200",
                                                "sense_id": "eb0b169d-8ba4-3c24-a302-6a4397da3e53",
                                                "text": "Русская народная поэзия имеет в себе целый обширный отдел песен разбойнических, содержанием для которых служит дикий и необузданный разгул человека, почувствовавшего себя без узды."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "92cc74ec-f20c-3fdc-9598-d1e2b2485f71",
                                        "entry_id": "8f41dded-98a8-339e-a1dc-99bdf3b054dd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "буйное, безудержное веселье с кутежами, попойками"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b73d40ca-c196-4713-a515-67feebd42334",
                                                "sense_id": "92cc74ec-f20c-3fdc-9598-d1e2b2485f71",
                                                "text": "Ночь улетала в диком разгуле; многие, упившись вином, спали у догоравших костров, другие ещё не спали, но и не замечали, как на небе несколько раз скралась луна."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "722c4fc9-2d6b-4656-82fe-c73bb5d9b34d",
                                                "sense_id": "92cc74ec-f20c-3fdc-9598-d1e2b2485f71",
                                                "text": "Но в Киеве вместо того, чтобы остепениться и начать новую жизнь, я снова предался кутежам и разгулу, так что отцовского наследства хватило мне не на долго."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
